	(text "The Arduino CNC Shield V3 snaps on top\nof the Arduino MEGA2560 board and leaves \nthe large double row connector exposed.\nThis is the connection points for the LCD\nand encoder, as well as anything else in\nthe future.  The CNC shield obtains all \npower except the motor supply from the \nArduino MEGA2560 board. The bulk 5V supply\nis obtained from a separate DC/DC converter\nthat derives 5V from the 24v motor supply."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 33.528 136.652 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4526e25a-7571-4766-b625-8c6879e1a6c9")
	)
	(text "Note: The Z-Axis could be used in the future for a wire tensioner."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 301.752 126.746 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "49e4389a-8a18-4997-afac-bd933a61687d")
	)
	(text "The rotary encoder with switch is used to make selections and to enter winding \nparameters. The lcd is for user interaction, and is a 4X20 LCD character display\nbased on the HD44780 Hitachi controller."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.274 216.408 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "79bf6539-8278-4bb9-9a5a-1f93ddc75270")
	)
	(text "M1 is the form or spindle motor.  This needs to have considerable\ntorque.  Use a NEMA 23 series motor for this motor.  If the motor\nrequires more current than the A4988 drivers (about 2A) can deliver\nyou will need to use a dedicated driver module such as a DM556. \nNo software changes should be required.\n\nM2 is the wire guide motor and a mid-size NEMA 17 motor will work\nfine.  I used an ACT 17HS series motor with 64 oz-in holding torque\nsuccessfully. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 348.234 82.804 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b16b4c08-7c77-4c5a-ad2e-1ffd18002b19")
	)
	(text "NOTE: If you must use an external stepper driver such as the DM556\ndo NOT populate the A4988 slot for the X drive on the CNC board.  DO \nNOT USE the A4988 driver AND the DM556 together."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.218 198.882 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c57b5443-e37b-42d9-9950-1f43a20358dd")
	)
